        "bodyText": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?><response><records><article xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><front><article-meta><title-group><article-title>Single-cell multi-omics benchmark for regulatory inference</article-title></title-group><permissions><license license-type=\"open-access\" xlink:href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\"><license-p>Open Access CC BY 4.0</license-p></license></permissions><abstract><p>We benchmark single-cell gene regulatory inference across six tissues using paired chromatin and RNA measurements.</p></abstract></article-meta></front><body><sec id=\"Sec1\"><title>Background</title><p>Regulatory network reconstruction from single-cell assays remains sensitive to sparsity and batch effects.</p></sec><sec id=\"Sec2\"><title>Methods</title><sec id=\"Sec3\"><title>Preprocessing</title><p>Cells with fewer than 500 detected transcripts were removed prior to normalization.</p></sec><sec id=\"Sec4\"><title>Evaluation Metrics</title><p>Precision-recall area under the curve was computed against ChIP-seq gold standards.</p></sec></sec><sec id=\"Sec5\"><title>Results</title><p>Joint ATAC+RNA models improved early precision by 34% compared with RNA-only baselines.</p></sec></body></article></records></response>",
